<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Rusplats worker sacking upheld, mine calm.</title>
<headline>Rusplats worker sacking upheld, mine calm.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>An employee at South Africa's Rustenburg Platinum Holdings Ltd, whose dismissal helped spark last week's wildcat strike by 4,600 mine workers, has failed in a bid to keep his job.</p>
<p>&quot;He's had his appeal and the original dismissal was upheld,&quot; Johan Adler, spokesman for holding company Anglo American Platinum Corp Ltd, said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The worker had been sacked on fraud charges 10 days ago.</p>
<p>Adler said there had been no reaction by workers at the Rustenburg mine -- the world's largest platinum producer -- with morning shift operations normal.</p>
<p>Last week's two-day strike affected 15 percent of production at Rusplats, which produced 690,000 ounces of platinum in the six months to December 1996.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482-1003</p>
</text>
